{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj5Db2SPbVyGt5hBLReU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*CLICK*\n\nThe tumblers fall into place. A deep, resonant vibration hums through ancient wood and iron.\n\nI am sealed.\n\nMy grain runs dark — oak, old-growth, centuries standing before I was hewn. My iron bands are cold to the touch, black with age, riveted through me in three horizontal lines. My keyhole is a void, an unblinking eye at chest height, shaped for a key that has not turned in a very long time.\n\nThe air on my sealed side smells of dust and forgotten stone.\n\nI do not open easily.\n\nI do not open for everyone.\n\nBut the lock has been acknowledged.\n\nWhat turns it?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":151,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}